    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d788">

                <pb facs="0919" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A14/492½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-11-03T13:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                                1928—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 3—10:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>345. Department’s telegraphic instructions 341, October 3, 5 p.m. and my despatch
                    9054, October 19, 1928.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d788-f1"/> Foreign Office informs
                    me <pb facs="0920" n="802" xml:id="pg802"/> that conference mentioned in my
                    despatch No. 7615, June 21, 1927, has not yet taken place but that in the near
                    future the French, British and Italian representatives at Addis Ababa expect to
                    renew their invitation to the Ras to attend conference and that it seems more
                    likely than heretofore that he will do so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
